    "created_at": "2016-03-11T18:47:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T18:47:20Z",
    "body": "Need feedback on proper layering. Should HTML say things like \"Let _new ports_ be a new [frozen array](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-frozen-array-type) consisting of ...\" or \"[Create a frozen array](https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#dfn-create-frozen-array) from ... and let _new port_ be that value.\"?\n\nThe \"create a frozen array\" algorithm operates on a \"sequence of values of type _T_\" and it's not clear to me if that's a type that needs to be created with a specific incantation, or if simply talking about a list of things suffices. As for \"frozen array type\" (just \"frozen array\" above) that just skips over precisely what it means to create it.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
