    "created_at": "2016-03-11T22:08:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-11T22:08:10Z",
    "body": "> Need feedback on proper layering. Should HTML say things like \"Let new ports be a new frozen array consisting of ...\" or \"Create a frozen array from ... and let new port be that value.\"?\n\nI think the former. Because...\n\n> The \"create a frozen array\" algorithm operates on a \"sequence of values of type T\" and it's not clear to me if that's a type that needs to be created with a specific incantation, or if simply talking about a list of things suffices.\n\nIt seems like that's specifically about `sequence<T>`, given the link to \"convert\".\n\n> As for \"frozen array type\" (just \"frozen array\" above) that just skips over precisely what it means to create it.\n\nRight, it appears this is the case for pretty much every Web IDL type (including normal `sequence<T>`s). So just vague language seems reasonable.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
